Hypothesis: the target's basis omitted the q=0 terms (mirroring the b=0
forms, which carry no constant term in either block), and its failure count
was taken over r=0..60 INCLUDING the fit points.

 p  b |        q>=0 basis (mine) |               q>=1 basis
------------------------------------------------------------
 2  0 |        0/61 fail (5 pts) |                 singular
 2  1 |        0/61 fail (5 pts) |                 singular
 2  2 |       56/61 fail (5 pts) |                 singular
 2  3 |       56/61 fail (5 pts) |                 singular
 3  0 |        0/61 fail (7 pts) |                 singular
 3  1 |        0/61 fail (7 pts) |                 singular
 3  2 |       54/61 fail (7 pts) |                 singular
 3  3 |       54/61 fail (7 pts) |                 singular

Target reports 54-56 failures out of 61, at p=2 AND p=3, for b=1,2,3.
61-5=56 (p=2: 5 fit points) and 61-7=54 (p=3: 7 fit points): i.e. every
out-of-sample point failed and only the fit points passed -- the signature
of a basis that cannot represent the true answer at all.
